[Verse 1]
Rain against a different window,
Power cable on the floor.
Fresh install and borrowed speakers,
Cardboard leaning by the door.
Clone the repo, check the changes,
There’s my name beside a date.
Found the alias I’d forgotten
For a path I used to hate.
[Pre-Chorus]
Before I find the coffee cups,
Tokyo Night is lighting up.
That shade of blue against the rain—
My fingers find their way again.
[Chorus]
Dotfiles,
Little things I carry.
Hidden in the home directory.
New walls,
Same light on the keys.
Bring a little of the old place
Here with me.
[Verse 2]
Oh-Mah-Chee, the morning after,
Windows falling into place.
Learn the keys, then change a couple,
Give the letters breathing space.
There’s a script from two jobs back,
Seven lines that earn their stay.
And a note that says “temporary,”
Still here working every day.
[Pre-Chorus]
Some of this is someone else’s,
Some I’ve shaped to fit my hands.
Some I leave until the weekend—
There’s a line that breaks my plans.
[Chorus]
Dotfiles,
Little things I carry.
Hidden in the home directory.
New walls,
Same light on the keys.
Bring a little of the old place
Here with me.
[Instrumental — Rhodes, shuffled drums, soft synth melody]
[Verse 3]
Lost an hour on a color,
Put it back the way it was.
Told myself it helped me focus.
Maybe I just liked the pause.
Now a friend has seen the screenshot,
Wants to try the setup too.
Take my local paths and fix them,
Write a note to walk them through.
[Bridge — intimate, sparse]
There’s a comment near the bottom
From a stranger years ago.
I was stuck there on a Sunday.
They explained it nice and slow.
Kept their name beside the answer,
Sent it with the rest tonight.
Somewhere else, another window,
Someone getting things just right.
[Final Chorus]
Dotfiles,
Little things we carry.
Hidden in the home directory.
New walls,
Same light on the keys.
Take a little of the old place—
Make it what you need.
Dotfiles,
Leave a little room.
Change the parts
That don’t feel like you.
Save it,
Let the evening breathe.
There’s a little of my old place
Keeping time with me.
[Outro]
Found the cups.
The room feels right.
Rain on the glass.
Tokyo Night.
